; C++ (ECIL 1.2, slice S1 review): a covariant result whose class D2 : R1, R2 is
; dynamic but whose vtable facts are not needed here (its constructor and
; destructor are in the other unit): X::get, in a secondary base position of
; X : P, Q, overrides Q::get and returns D2* for R2*, so its thunk adjusts
; both this and the result (_ZTchn16_h16_N1X3getEv: this -16, result +16).
;   struct X : P, Q { D2 *get() override; };  struct D2 : R1, R2 { D2(); ~D2(); };
